 Chem||274|32099||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10542244</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lai</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Harnish</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Chadwick</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estrogen receptor alpha inhibits IL-1beta induction of gene expression in the mouse liver</article-title><source>Endocrinology</source><year>2002</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>2559</fpage><lpage>2570</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Endocrinology||143|2559||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12072388</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bigsby</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nephew</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The NEDD8 pathway is required for proteasome-mediated degradation of human estrogen receptor (ER)-alpha and essential for the antiproliferative activity of ICI 182&#x02009;780 in ERalpha-positive breast cancer cells</article-title><source>Mol Endocrinol</source><year>2003</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>356</fpage><lpage>365</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Endocrinol||17|356||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12554766</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Filardo</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Quinn</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>KI</given-names></name><name><surname>Frackelton</surname><given-names>AR</given-n